================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

RWKV-LM and the RWKV-4-Pile-169M weights
  Upstream: https://github.com/BlinkDL/RWKV-LM
  Used:     The pretrained RWKV-4-Pile-169M model weights are baked into
            the Docker image and distributed unmodified. Inference uses
            the `rwkv` pip package from the same author, which provides
            the fast WKV CUDA kernel that our compression pipeline depends
            on.
  License:  Apache-2.0.

constriction
  Upstream: https://github.com/bamler-lab/constriction
  Used:     Range / ANS arithmetic coding of next-token distributions.
            Loaded via the `constriction` pip package.
  License:  MIT.

PyTorch + Hugging Face tokenizers
  Standard transitive Python dependencies of the inference path.
  Licenses: BSD-3-Clause (PyTorch), Apache-2.0 (tokenizers).

L3TC — Leveraging RWKV for Learned Lossless Low-Complexity Text Compression
  Upstream: https://github.com/alipay/L3TC-leveraging-rwkv-for-learned-lossless-low-complexity-text-compression
  Paper:    Zhao et al., AAAI 2025 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.16642)
  Used:     krunch's architectural shape (RWKV LM logits → arithmetic
            coder, per-chunk encoding with state reset at chunk
            boundaries) is descended from the L3TC reference. krunch
            diverged on the deterministic encoder/decoder path, 24-bit
            AC, self-describing blob format, B>1 batched stepped decoder,
            single Docker image, and dynamic chunking. See
            docs/PEER_CODEC_NOTES.md §0 for the lineage delta.
  License:  Apache-2.0.

Nacrith-GPU
  Upstream: https://github.com/robtacconelli/Nacrith-GPU
  Used:     `krunch/codec/adaptive_head.py` is a direct numpy port of
            Nacrith-GPU's `adaptive_head.py` (the fp64 per-document
            online bias correction algorithm + identical
            adjust/update semantics). `krunch/codec/adaptive_head_gpu.py`
            is the torch fp64 GPU mirror of the same algorithm, byte-
            exact with the CPU port. Currently parked behind
            KRUNCH_ADAPTIVE_HEAD=1 (see docs/OPTIMIZATIONS.md §4).
  License:  Apache-2.0.

rwkv-cpp-accelerated
  Upstream: https://github.com/harrisonvanderbyl/rwkv-cpp-accelerated
  Used:     Kernel-layout patterns referenced when designing krunch's
            RWKV-4 CUDA kernels (uint8 weights with per-input-channel
            scale/offset, 3-way fused KVR matmul launch shape, RWKV
            state buffer layout). See docs/PEER_CODEC_NOTES.md §4 for
            the technique trace. krunch's kernels were written from
            scratch with WMMA + cp.async on top of these patterns;
            no code copied verbatim.
  License:  Apache-2.0.
